.TH "PB-DAEMON-DEVICE-GUARD-INSTALL" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-daemon-device-guard-install - Install the root-owned device guard service


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb daemon device-guard install [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Install the root-owned device guard service

.PP
Install the root-owned guard service and its protected loopback range. --loopback-cidr selects the permitted local range; review it before changing host integration.

.PP
The device guard is a privileged local helper for protected device-name resolution. Installation and removal change local operating-system integration; use the dedicated service commands for the ordinary Paperboat daemon.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for install

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--loopback-cidr\fP=""
	validated local device loopback /16


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	configuration file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	Paperboat server URL


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-daemon-device-guard(1)\fP
